      "verdict": "FAIL",
      "reason": "measured 3, but expected = 1",
      "feedback": "The debounce logic in loop() (sketch.ino:27) only blocks re-toggling for LOCKOUT_MS=200ms after the last toggle, but it never waits for the button to actually go HIGH (released) again. Since the simulated bouncy press keeps BUTTON_PIN LOW for longer than 200ms, once the lockout window expires the condition on line 27 is true again (still LOW), so the LED toggles a second and third time (ON->OFF->ON) during what should be a single press. Fix by requiring a release (or a stable LOW read over a short debounce interval) before allowing the next toggle, rather than just waiting out a fixed lockout timer.",
      "code_location": "sketch.ino:27",
      "cause_found": true,
      "same_cause_as": null
    },
